factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The caption's 'நடவடிக்கை' (action) line presents the counting work as a police-style 'action' led by Chandran, which is a framing not in the article.
  The reel_script's first sentence says the offering was made 'in Namakkal temples' (நாமக்கல் கோயில் உண்டியல்களில்), which is a loose generalisation of the three named temples' hundis, not an exact statement of the article.
  The slides_spec 'எங்கே' slide lists 'ஆஞ்சனேயர் கோயில் பக்தர்கள் தங்கும் மண்டபத்தில்' but the hl1 headline says 'நாமக்கல் கோயில் உண்டியலில்' and the tamil_headline says 'ஆஞ்சனேயர் கோயில் உண்டியலில்', so the headline attributes all 13 hundis to Anjaneyar temple while the article says the three temples' hundis were opened there, creating a mixed attribution.
  The caption's 'Namakkal Anjaneyar temple hundi offerings' English line and headline together imply the whole Rs 62 lakh is from Anjaneyar temple alone, while the article says the amount is from the 13 hundis of three temples (Narasimha, Anjaneyar, Ranganathar).
  The reel_script omits that the counting was done by students of a private college in Tiruchengode only partly: it does mention them, so no omission here, but the caption and reel do not clarify the count was overseen by the Assistant Commissioner (in-charge) as the article states in the reel; the reel says 'உதவி ஆணையர் சந்திரன்' without the '(பொறுப்பு)' qualifier, a minor deviation from the article.
