  The reel_script and caption say livestock deaths occurred ('கால்நடைகள் உயிரிழந்துள்ளன' / 'கால்நடைகள் உயிரிழந்துள்ளன' in reel) and link them to the 5-year damage, which matches the article, but the reel omits that the vaccination is a precaution, which is acceptable; however, the reel_script's 'கடந்த 5 ஆண்டுகளாக இந்நோயால் பெரும் பாதிப்பு ஏற்பட்டு, கால்நடைகள் உயிரிழந்துள்ளன' merges two separate facts into one sentence, and the slide 'நோயின் தாக்கம்' presents the 5-year impact as the disease's damage without the article's causal link to the precautionary vaccination.
  The slide line 'வெப்பம், கனமழையால் கால்நடைகளைப் பராமரிப்பது கடினம்' is attributed under the 'விவசாயிகளின்' heading, which is a truncated and ungrammatical title that leaves the slide's meaning unclear.
  The reel_script states the disease 'பெரும்பாலும் எருமைகளைத் தாக்குவதில்லை' accurately, but the reel and caption describe the vaccination as 'முகாம்' in the headline while the article describes it as an ongoing drive across surrounding areas; the headline's 'முகாம் தீவிரம்' mixes a camp with an intensified drive, which is two different facts in one phrase.
  The reel_script's statement that the grant request is for 'கொட்டகை அமைக்க' is correct, but the article's point that rural areas receive such grants, while the urban request is the subject, is omitted, leaving the grant demand without its comparative context.
